WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.480
When you absolutely, positively have to have
Jonah Hill for your tentpole picture, be prepared

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:07.160
to pony up some major cash.

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:11.820
The star, who is in talks to appear in writer/director
Matt Reeves' The Batman in an undisclosed

00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:16.369
role, is reportedly seeking a figure equivalent
to twice what the flick's star Robert Pattinson

00:00:16.369 --> 00:00:17.260
will pull down.

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:19.600
"Uh, don't forget about my money."

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:24.499
Variety film reporter Justin Kroll disclosed
the tidbit on Twitter, adding some context

00:00:24.499 --> 00:00:27.080
to the news that Hill is being eyed for a
role in The Batman.

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:31.089
Exactly which role that is has been kept under
wraps by studio Warner Brothers, but it's

00:00:31.089 --> 00:00:35.100
been speculated by many that the star could
be cast as the Riddler or the Penguin.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:37.220
According to Kroll, this is dead accurate.

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:38.100
Kroll wrote,

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:42.200
"So on the Jonah front, he's had the offer
for over a month and besides money being a

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:46.810
bargaining point (at one point heard he wanted
10 which is wild since Rob isn't making half

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:50.470
that) but also which character he would play,
whether its the Riddler or Penguin."

00:00:50.470 --> 00:00:52.220
There's quite a bit to unpack there.

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:56.040
Kroll states that Hill has been sitting on
a firm offer for more than a month, which

00:00:56.050 --> 00:01:00.350
could be taken to mean that while he's still
technically "in talks" for the role negotiations

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:01.420
have stalled somewhat.

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:05.860
The reporter also asserts that at one point,
Hill was asking for a whopping $10 million

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:08.880
dollar payday to appear in The Batman, but
it can be inferred that he's not going to

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:09.800
get it.

00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:13.220
If Warner Brothers were cool with coughing
up his reported asking price, there would

00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:16.160
be no reason for Hill to have been sitting
on their offer for this long.

00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:17.520
"I'm not understanding.

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:19.620
How much money you make?"

00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:23.920
It's likely that the studio countered with
a figure more in line with what Pattinson

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:27.600
will be making, which Kroll says isn't even
half of $10 million dollars.

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:29.320
It has to be pretty close, though.

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:34.119
Superhero salaries for a first solo picture
tend to fall within the $3-to-$5 million dollar

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:37.940
range, and it's safe to say that Batman is
a pretty high-profile property.

00:01:37.940 --> 00:01:42.520
By way of comparison, it's been reported that
Brie Larson was paid $5 million dollars

00:01:42.530 --> 00:01:47.149
to star in 2019’s Captain Marvel, while
Benedict Cumberbatch pulled down right around

00:01:47.149 --> 00:01:50.120
$3 million dollars to lead 2016's Doctor Strange.

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:54.600
We haven't even gotten to the last part of
Kroll's tweet, which is perhaps the most interesting

00:01:54.609 --> 00:01:58.750
of all: apparently, a major sticking point
between Hill and Warner Brothers has to do

00:01:58.750 --> 00:02:02.670
with which character he'll be playing, which
could imply that the two parties aren't seeing

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:04.340
eye to eye on the matter.

00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:06.119
"I'm not stupid.

00:02:06.119 --> 00:02:07.119
I'm smart.

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:09.360
I make million dollar deals."

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:13.220
Physically speaking, the Penguin would be
the most obvious role for Hill, since the

00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:15.520
actor is relatively short at 5-foot-7.

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:19.840
He lost a significant amount of weight back
in 2011, so he's not the Oswald Copperpot

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:22.680
of the comics, but he still can't shake the
fat jokes …

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:28.520
"When Jonah's agent told him that Quentin
Tarantino wanted him to be in a spaghetti

00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:31.060
western, Jonah was like, 'You had me at spaghetti.'"

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:35.800
It seems likely that the Penguin is the role
that Warner Brothers has in mind for the actor,

00:02:35.810 --> 00:02:39.710
while Hill, perhaps sensitive about his weight,
is more keen to take a crack at portraying

00:02:39.710 --> 00:02:43.240
Edward Nygma, the Riddler which seems like
a pretty good fit to us.

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:48.140
Hill may be known primarily for his comedic
roles, but he is a gifted, Academy Award-nominated

00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:52.290
actor, and we can absolutely see him bringing
just the right notes of cunning and madness

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:53.360
to the role of Nygma.

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:57.520
Reeves has said that he'll be fielding a more
grounded, noir -influenced take on Batman

00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:01.420
than previous filmmakers, so while it may
seem a little on the nose to cast a comedic

00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:05.020
actor as the Riddler, Hill has proven that
he has the chops to to add a bit of comedic

00:03:05.020 --> 00:03:07.280
flavor to the role without overwhelming it.

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:11.140
It remains to be seen how the month-long stalemate
between actor and studio will be resolved,

00:03:11.140 --> 00:03:13.040
or indeed, if it will be at all.

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:17.340
It's obvious that Hill and Warner Brothers
began their negotiations pretty far apart

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:20.840
on what the details of the actor's contract
would be, and it's not like there aren't dozens

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:24.390
of thespians in Hollywood who would fall all
over themselves for the chance to play either

00:03:24.390 --> 00:03:26.740
of the roles Hill is reportedly being eyed
for.

00:03:26.740 --> 00:03:30.640
Of course, we'll be keeping our eyes peeled
for any developments, and we'll keep you up

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:31.440
to speed.

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:35.631
The Batman is expected to begin production
late this year or early next, and the flick

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:38.940
swoops into theaters on June 25th, 2021.

